WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.545
(Water lapping gently)

00:00:03.545 --> 00:00:05.631
The Lord is with me.

00:00:05.631 --> 00:00:07.507
I will not be afraid.

00:00:09.426 --> 00:00:12.054
What can a mere man do to me?

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:13.847
(Door slams)

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:16.225
The door is kicked in,
overseers storm inside,

00:00:16.225 --> 00:00:18.143
seize Peter, who violently
resists.

00:00:18.143 --> 00:00:19.853
Overseer: 
I said now, boy.

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:21.188
Peter: 
Do not touch me!

00:00:21.355 --> 00:00:22.856
Scipion moves into help.

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:23.607
Scipion:
Papa!

00:00:24.191 --> 00:00:24.858
Adam Stephenson:
Betsy cries.

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:25.734
Get back, boy!

00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:27.236
(Fighting Noise)

00:00:27.236 --> 00:00:27.945
Sheer chaos.

00:00:28.362 --> 00:00:28.987
Peter:
Help!

00:00:31.573 --> 00:00:35.077
This was without
question the hardest film

00:00:35.077 --> 00:00:38.247
of my entire career.

00:00:39.164 --> 00:00:43.794
I live in doubt from
the moment I say "yes"

00:00:43.794 --> 00:00:47.839
to a character until a magic
moment.

00:00:47.839 --> 00:00:51.635
Will Smith:
There's a magic moment of
comprehension,

00:00:51.635 --> 00:00:54.054
Will Smith:
and you never know when

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:58.308
that magic moment is going to
show up.

00:01:02.521 --> 00:01:07.442
Dresser:
They arrive at the Rebel camp
still barefoot.

00:01:07.442 --> 00:01:10.070
-Barefoot, okay, that'll
be fine, that'll work.
-Okay.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.238
That'll definitely work.

00:01:14.116 --> 00:01:15.075
Dresser:
If you want to at
this point..

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:16.451
Man On Left: 
He's tricked out.

00:01:16.451 --> 00:01:17.661
Man:
I think it's gonna be easier
for

00:01:17.661 --> 00:01:19.121
whoever's putting it on him.

00:01:19.121 --> 00:01:19.830
How does that feel?

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:26.461
Man:
We're hoping that that
will always go over the...

00:01:28.338 --> 00:01:29.298
Man:
You'll have this little box.

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:36.930
Man:
Yeah, yeah, come
underneath.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.390
There you go, come underneath
first.

00:01:39.725 --> 00:01:41.351
Man:
Get your head out of there if
it's starting to waggle out.

00:01:44.855 --> 00:01:45.856
Yeah, that's nice.

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:48.608
Whoa.

00:01:51.194 --> 00:01:56.616
Will Smith:
It turns off... your... agency.

00:01:57.284 --> 00:01:59.536
You don't want to step,
you don't wanna move,

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.664
you don't wanna look anybody in
the face.

00:02:02.664 --> 00:02:05.584
It's deeply dehumanizing.

00:02:05.584 --> 00:02:09.296
It's like in the most basic,

00:02:09.296 --> 00:02:11.882
simple textures of human
interaction,

00:02:11.882 --> 00:02:13.800
you just, you turn it off.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.178
You just turn it off, you know.

00:02:16.928 --> 00:02:20.932
It's a, it's gonna be a long,
hard summer.

00:02:20.932 --> 00:02:24.519
♪♪

00:02:24.519 --> 00:02:28.357
Pierce Austin:
Hair is, I think, is
paramount and essential

00:02:28.357 --> 00:02:32.194
Pierce Austin:
to the character I'm hoping to
create.

00:02:32.194 --> 00:02:37.074
A man who is strong, a
man who has integrity,

00:02:37.074 --> 00:02:41.578
Pierce Austin:
and a man who has had a very
rough life, to say the least.

00:02:44.706 --> 00:02:50.170
Pierce Austin:
The shape has to be flattering,
but it has to tell a story

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:52.214
Pierce Austin:
that he's never seen any vanity
before.

00:02:52.214 --> 00:02:54.299
Pierce Austin:
He doesn't know vanity.

00:02:54.299 --> 00:02:56.927
Will Smith:
Pierce Austin, my hair
stylist,

00:02:56.927 --> 00:02:59.096
did such a brilliant job.

00:02:59.096 --> 00:03:03.016
It's like nobody notices
that that's a wig.

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:08.021
Will Smith:
It's a wig that disappears
in the mind of the audience,

00:03:08.814 --> 00:03:13.819
but it's so critical in
delivering the character

00:03:14.778 --> 00:03:19.533
and, you know, touching that
space inside of the audience.

00:03:19.533 --> 00:03:24.538
How his hair looks is so
critical, yet it disappears.

00:03:24.538 --> 00:03:30.669
♪♪

00:03:30.669 --> 00:03:34.131
Will Smith:
Hair and makeup and wardrobe is
always one

00:03:34.131 --> 00:03:38.051
Will Smith:
of the first thresholds for
me to fall into character.

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:42.597
Will Smith:
You know, once I see myself in
the mirror,

00:03:42.597 --> 00:03:44.891
Will Smith:
it transforms your thoughts and
feelings.

00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:47.227
Will Smith:
It changes how you walk.

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:49.688
Will Smith:
It changes how to hold my mouth.

00:03:49.688 --> 00:03:52.524
The makeup definitely
intensifies

00:03:52.524 --> 00:03:56.361
whatever Peter is experiencing
that day,

00:03:56.361 --> 00:03:59.364
Judy Murdock:
and I have to keep that in mind
every day.

00:03:59.364 --> 00:04:01.491
Peter, coming into
the construction camp,

00:04:01.491 --> 00:04:05.245
this the first time he arrives
to this slave encampment

00:04:05.245 --> 00:04:07.372
where he's been abducted from
his family.

00:04:07.873 --> 00:04:09.082
Director: 
Alright let's clear the set,
please.

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:11.209
Director:
Let's stand by, picture will be
next.

00:04:11.209 --> 00:04:14.045
♪♪

00:04:14.045 --> 00:04:18.925
Will Smith:
That Confederate War camp
is one of the best designed

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:22.262
and most accurate sets I've ever
been on.

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:28.560
(Hammers clinking)

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:29.436
(Horse whinnies)

00:04:30.228 --> 00:04:31.646
Will Smith:
All of the sound.

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:38.028
The life of the camp got
created.

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:40.614
Will Smith:
You can feel the pain.

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:44.826
Will Smith:
You can feel the suffering.

00:04:44.826 --> 00:04:48.663
Will Smith:
It's like the walls are talking
to you.

00:04:48.663 --> 00:04:52.459
Will Smith:
It made it that much more
difficult to emotionally depict,

00:04:52.459 --> 00:04:56.421
but as an actor, it was
spectacular to be surrounded

00:04:56.421 --> 00:04:58.798
and immersed in that way.

00:05:00.008 --> 00:05:02.010
So it's the same thing, with a
thin shield

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:04.137
on the outside with some color.

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:05.764
They should fit.

00:05:05.764 --> 00:05:06.598
How do they feel?

00:05:07.516 --> 00:05:08.475
Not bad.

00:05:08.475 --> 00:05:11.186
And yeah, they always help
with dialect anyway, so...

00:05:13.146 --> 00:05:14.898
Good to see you, how are you
doing?

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:16.316
Arron Speiser:
You want to hear the dialogue?

00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:18.401
- Is that what's the difference
between that and the others?
- Yeah, there is dialogue.

00:05:18.401 --> 00:05:21.947
Steady yourself, long day out
here.

00:05:21.947 --> 00:05:25.617
Steady yourself, steady
yourself.

00:05:25.617 --> 00:05:28.662
Will Smith:
Steady yourself, a long day out
here.

00:05:28.662 --> 00:05:32.457
Will Smith:
A long day out here, a long day
out here.

00:05:32.457 --> 00:05:35.418
Steady yourself, a long day out
here.

00:05:35.418 --> 00:05:39.506
The dialect is a major
part of the storytelling.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:42.801
This is just work.

00:05:43.927 --> 00:05:46.054
Peter:
Same as you always done.

00:05:46.054 --> 00:05:50.517
Will Smith:
Peter's dialect is Haitian
Creole.

00:05:50.517 --> 00:05:54.020
Will Smith:
Just prior to the Haitian
Revolution,

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:56.898
the slave owners were escaping

00:05:56.898 --> 00:06:00.443
and they were coming to America.

00:06:00.443 --> 00:06:06.741
A huge Haitian contingent
came into that Louisiana area.

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:11.997
Will Smith:
So Haitian French was
the best guesstimate of

00:06:11.997 --> 00:06:14.541
what Peter probably spoke.

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:20.630
I do not know why God shows
Himself

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:25.468
to some people and not to
others.

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:31.141
But if you do not know Him,

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:40.525
I will pray for you.

00:06:42.777 --> 00:06:45.614
Will Smith:
Peter's spirituality was one

00:06:45.614 --> 00:06:50.577
Will Smith:
of the most interesting
explorations for me to understand

00:06:51.036 --> 00:06:56.041
Will Smith:
how someone can survive
this level of brutality,

00:06:56.958 --> 00:06:59.210
Will Smith:
this level of suffering.

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:01.546
And it came down to Peter's
faith.

00:07:04.674 --> 00:07:06.801
Will Smith:
You learn all your lines,
you learn your dialect,

00:07:06.801 --> 00:07:09.429
Will Smith:
you get your hair, you get your
makeup, you, you know

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:12.307
Will Smith:
you rehearse with some
of the other actors,

00:07:12.307 --> 00:07:14.059
Will Smith:
you do all of those things,

00:07:14.059 --> 00:07:17.187
but what could give a person the
fortitude

00:07:17.187 --> 00:07:21.816
and the endurance to be able to
sustain

00:07:21.816 --> 00:07:26.154
Will Smith:
with that level of
violence and malevolence,

00:07:26.154 --> 00:07:29.574
and, you know, God was the only
answer.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:40.543
Will Smith:
There's a magical moment when
you understand a character

00:07:40.585 --> 00:07:43.004
Will Smith:
in a non-intellectual way.

00:07:43.004 --> 00:07:45.548
Will Smith:
There was an interesting
thing in Peter's writings

00:07:45.548 --> 00:07:47.842
Will Smith:
where he had been beaten into a
coma

00:07:47.842 --> 00:07:51.638
Will Smith:
and he had been unconscious for
months.

00:07:51.638 --> 00:07:55.975
And when he comes out, he
talks about having met God.

00:07:55.975 --> 00:08:02.065
He heard and cultivated
a relationship with God.

00:08:02.107 --> 00:08:04.359
Will Smith:
He felt like he knew God.

00:08:04.359 --> 00:08:08.154
Will Smith:
So he had gone beyond faith into
a place

00:08:08.154 --> 00:08:10.281
Will Smith:
that few of us get to visit.

00:08:12.909 --> 00:08:16.621
Will Smith:
I just, I love working to
understand the mindset of that,

00:08:16.621 --> 00:08:18.206
Will Smith:
that kind of character.

00:08:19.165 --> 00:08:21.668
It's not a movie about
slavery,...

00:08:21.668 --> 00:08:25.255
♪♪

00:08:25.255 --> 00:08:26.923
Will Smith:
...it's a movie about freedom...

00:08:26.923 --> 00:08:28.717
♪♪

00:08:28.717 --> 00:08:31.136
Will Smith:
... and the power of faith

00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:38.435
Will Smith:
combined with love... being
invincible.

